# Checker gap: a field read on a value that may be a fieldless marker is
# accepted, and fails at run time.
#
# `probe/probe` answers `hit` or `miss`, and only `hit` has a field `t`.
# `kanso check` says ok; running says
#   error[runtime]: `miss` has no field `t`
#
# The checker refuses the equivalent read when the alternative is `none`
# ("this can be a none and ... has no arm for it") and when it is an err;
# a marker that stands in for none, which chapter 04 recommends, gets no
# such check. Expected: a refusal at check time naming `miss`.
import "./probe"

print "{(probe/probe 0).t}"
